# wip — plan-ecology-clustering
# Branch: feature/plan-ecology-clustering
# Started: 2026-03-27

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["roots"]{
 @cluster: ~".agents/plans/plan-ecology-clustering/plan-ecology-clustering.spw"
 @plan: ~".agents/plans/plan-ecology-clustering/PLAN.md"
 @artifact: ~".agents/plans/plan-ecology-clustering/plan-ecology-clustering.spw"
 @pattern: ~".spw/patterns/literate-ui.spw"
 @topography: ~".agents/plans/operational-topography/operational-topography.spw"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Recluster the active plans so execution, contributor formation, research, and speculative work stop competing for one urgency queue. Each plan should gain a clearer learning value, discussion subject, and experimental question."
 ~#taste: "clarity, layering, naming, meaningfulness"
}

^["development"]{
 lane: #execution_truth
 ladder: #bridge
 develops: [#planning_judgment, #principal_engineering, #design_ladder, #ecology_taste]
 review_surfaces: [@cluster, @plan, @artifact, @pattern, @topography]
 snippet_routes: [#cluster_tag, #commit_bar, #review_loop, #ladder_note]
}

^["concept_index"]{
 primary: [#clustering, #planning, #urgency, #learning, #research, #principal_engineering]
 surfaces: [#plans, #artifacts, #governance, #release, #curriculum]
 tensions: [#decorative_taxonomy, #stale_paths, #priority_blur, #learning_drag]
 transfers: [#language, #component, #page, #service]
}

^["recursive_improvement"]{
 loop: [
  "? reread active plans, artifacts, and repo patterns before widening the taxonomy",
  "< ship one clustering rule that changes scheduling, review, or commit judgment",
  "$ record what became more discussable, teachable, or indexable",
  "^ propagate the surviving doctrine into local plan memory and artifacts",
  "% keep the cluster map operational rather than decorative",
 ]
 gates: [#specificity, #review_value, #transfer, #non_ornamental]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-27 15:04] observe — the active plan ecology mixes release-critical lanes, contributor curricula, public-interest probes, and stale rewrite-era recoveries under one undifferentiated sense of urgency.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:05] decide — the recluster should preserve curricular value rather than demote it; learning lanes need a better role, not a quieter one.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:07] decide — every active plan gets three added readings: what it teaches, what it creates for discussion, and what research or probe it enables.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:08] revise — canopy and release plans should explicitly consume the cluster map so tags and launch claims depend on execution truth lanes, while curricula and research lanes still feed heuristics and discussion into the work.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:09] taste — a well-considered commit should make something truer, teach something, and open a better subject for conversation even before external demand is obvious.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:44] decide — the cluster doctrine should explicitly serve principal engineering: deepen design taste, web linguistics, and applied learning science rather than only sorting urgency.
 >>[2026-03-27 15:45] revise — add a learning ladder from Spw language design into component, page, and service design so plans can be valued for how they develop judgment, not just what they ship.
 >>[2026-03-27 16:02] observe — `.spw/patterns/literate-ui.spw` introduces a denser pattern idiom: operator-coded maps, embedded facet blocks, and wonder frames carrying relational explanation.
 >>[2026-03-27 16:03] revise — restyle the cluster artifact toward that idiom: fewer long prose strings, more operator-grouped structure, tag sets, and wonder routes between research, curriculum, execution, and design ladders.
 >>[2026-03-27 16:18] decide — the cluster artifact should become a richer review instrument: it needs explicit surfaces for code-pattern review, web-ecosystem capability review, syntax testing, and snippet discovery.
 >>[2026-03-27 16:19] taste — depth here should not mean more narration alone; it should mean more places where the repo can be queried, compared, and learned from.
 >>[2026-03-27 16:43] revise — propagate the cluster doctrine into representative ladder plans so the taxonomy becomes local judgment: language (`register-phase-evolution`), component (`vscode-register-explorer`), page (`curriculum-html-css-mastery`), and service (`runtime-dx-foundation`).
 >>[2026-03-27 16:44] taste — the doctrine is only real if individual plans gain review surfaces, capability transfer, syntax discipline, and snippet routes that can steer actual commits.
 >>[2026-03-27 17:12] revise — extend the propagation into the lagging curriculum/audit/editor-future plans and into companion `.spw` artifacts so the doctrine touches both human-facing plans and machine-readable interaction specs.
 >>[2026-03-27 17:13] taste — the remaining risk is lore-era placeholder paths pretending to be immediate work; when no concrete target exists, the plan should say so and redirect energy into review surfaces, snippets, and reusable judgments.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:36] observe — mounted consumer corpora may contain richer claim, audit, convention, and language surfaces than editor-parity plans anticipate.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:37] decide — mounted-consumer review becomes the ecology's primary transfer test: repository-local models use the pinned workbench as an instrument, keep findings consumer-owned, and return only deliberately distilled improvements upstream.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:38] revise — prioritize `spw-site-install`, review protocol, claim/probe portability, and governance evidence; keep editor-specific parity and migrations speculative until repeated consumer reviews demonstrate their utility.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:14] revise — register `mounted-consumer-tooling` as the identity-free audit bridge across CLI, LSP, and editor plans; retire named-domain fixtures from active plan evidence.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:20] register — operational-topography becomes the neutral bridge for parser-owned coordinates, evidence/effect grades, exact-first discovery, and differential authority; garden and LSP roadmap consume it in their declared lanes.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:21] revise — temperature is a dated snapshot rather than a derived fact, and repository authority no longer requires a claim-shaped surface.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:18] observe — ecology sweep at main@61025640. 55 active plans became 50: archived bias-resolution-product (merged, 17 done entries), neovim-spw-surfaces (complete, landed in b1439e0a), v030-release-prep (closed, v0.3.0 tagged), lsp-lore-upstream-bridge and skills-instrumentation-utility (both explicitly closed in their own streams).
 >>[2026-07-27 13:18] decide — four plans independently named one object: onf.ts "semantic hash", spw-garden-geometry "ONF shape hash", geometric-analysis-tooling "shapeFingerprint", apposition-cache-granules "granule key". Wrote .spw/patterns/surface-identity.spw to hold the shared vocabulary, distinguishing content_hash, shape_fingerprint, and granule_key by their collision semantics, and cross-referenced it from all four.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:18] observe — collision found and recorded rather than resolved: apposition-cache-granules and spw-beat-diff-precipitation both edit packages/spw-lsp/src/server-index.ts and both add a config block to .spw/workspace.spw. surface-identity.spw rules one shared cache block; ordering is still open.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:18] observe — five plans are stranded on the deleted src/ui, src/core, and src/platform layout: refactor-import-sprawl, symmetry-explorer-instrument, audit-css-tokens, audit-ui-data-models, audit-data-attributes. Marked stranded rather than archived — they were never declared done, and the UI concerns may belong to a site repo. brand-core-ids is separate: relocatable to packages/, and still wanted.
}

